# 4. File-roll configuration

Hourly partitions do not require one file per hour.

Files should roll inside each hourly partition based on time or size:

```properties
gg.handler.s3.maxFileSize=256m
gg.handler.s3.fileRollInterval=10m
gg.handler.s3.inactivityRollInterval=2m
gg.handler.s3.rollOnShutdown=true
gg.handler.s3.rollOnTruncate=true
```

Expected output:

```text
dptf_ingest_hour=10/
    file_1005.parquet
    file_1015.parquet
    file_1025.parquet
    file_1035.parquet
    file_1045.parquet
    file_1055.parquet
```

The first rollover condition reached causes the file to close. Oracle recommends combining size- and time-based rolling, avoiding very short intervals and targeting approximately 256–512 MB for analytical Parquet workloads. Oracle identifies 5–15 minutes as a typical near-real-time roll interval.

Initial values:

```text
Partition interval:         1 hour
File-roll interval:         10 minutes
Inactivity interval:         2 minutes
Maximum staging file size: 256 MB
Roll on shutdown:           true
Roll on truncate:           true
```

The final compressed Parquet objects may be smaller than the GoldenGate staging-file threshold. Measure final S3 file sizes and adjust after load testing.

