# 5. CDC record format

Use operation-oriented output because the raw layer must retain inserts, updates and deletes.

Operation-oriented output represents:

| Operation | Before image | After image |
| --------- | -----------: | ----------: |
| Insert    |           No |         Yes |
| Update    |          Yes |         Yes |
| Delete    |          Yes |          No |
| Truncate  |           No |          No |

Oracle documents this structure for operation-based formatting.

Conceptual raw Parquet schema:

```text
dptf_source_system
dptf_source_database
dptf_source_schema
dptf_source_table
dptf_source_object

dptf_operation_type
dptf_source_operation_ts
dptf_ingestion_ts

dptf_source_csn
dptf_source_transaction_id
dptf_transaction_operation_seq
dptf_trail_position
dptf_primary_keys
dptf_schema_changed
dptf_replicat_group

before
after
```

The `before` and `after` objects contain the actual Oracle table columns.

Example update:

```json
{
  "dptf_operation_type": "U",
  "dptf_source_object": "TRADE.EXECUTIONS",
  "dptf_source_csn": "123456789",
  "dptf_trail_position": "00000001230000124567",

  "before": {
    "EXECUTION_ID": 1001,
    "STATUS": "PENDING",
    "PRICE": 101.25
  },

  "after": {
    "EXECUTION_ID": 1001,
    "STATUS": "COMPLETED",
    "PRICE": 101.25
  }
}
```

