# 6. GoldenGate technical metadata

Configure the metadata field names using `metaColumnsTemplate`.

```properties
gg.handler.s3.format.metaColumnsTemplate=\
${static[dptf_source_system].oracle},\
${static[dptf_source_database].trading},\
${catalog[dptf_source_catalog]},\
${schema[dptf_source_schema]},\
${table[dptf_source_table]},\
${objectname[dptf_source_object]},\
${optype[dptf_operation_type]},\
${timestamp[dptf_source_operation_ts]},\
${currenttimestampiso8601[dptf_ingestion_ts]},\
${csn[dptf_source_csn]},\
${xid[dptf_source_transaction_id]},\
${opseqno[dptf_transaction_operation_seq]},\
${position[dptf_trail_position]},\
${primarykeysmap[dptf_primary_keys]},\
${metadatachanged[dptf_schema_changed]},\
${groupname[dptf_replicat_group]}
```

Oracle allows the output field name to be supplied in square brackets, which makes the `dptf_` naming convention possible.

## Field definitions

| Field                            | Meaning                                             |
| -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_source_system`             | Stable platform source identifier                   |
| `dptf_source_database`           | Stable Oracle database/PDB identifier               |
| `dptf_source_catalog`            | GoldenGate catalog value, where available           |
| `dptf_source_schema`             | Oracle schema                                       |
| `dptf_source_table`              | Oracle table                                        |
| `dptf_source_object`             | Fully qualified source table                        |
| `dptf_operation_type`            | `I`, `U`, `D` or `T`                                |
| `dptf_source_operation_ts`       | Timestamp carried by the trail record               |
| `dptf_ingestion_ts`              | Time GoldenGate formatted the event                 |
| `dptf_source_csn`                | Source commit sequence number                       |
| `dptf_source_transaction_id`     | Source Oracle transaction ID                        |
| `dptf_transaction_operation_seq` | Record sequence inside the transaction              |
| `dptf_trail_position`            | GoldenGate trail sequence and RBA                   |
| `dptf_primary_keys`              | Map containing primary-key names and values         |
| `dptf_schema_changed`            | True on the first operation after a metadata change |
| `dptf_replicat_group`            | GoldenGate Replicat group name                      |

Oracle documents these metacolumns, including CSN, transaction ID, transaction operation sequence, trail position, primary-key map and metadata-change indicator.

## Fixed GoldenGate fields

The operation formatter uses the fixed fields:

```text
before
after
```

It may also produce fields such as:

```text
PRICE_isMissing
```

GoldenGate uses `_isMissing` to distinguish:

```text
PRICE = null and PRICE_isMissing = false
```

meaning the source value was SQL `NULL`, from:

```text
PRICE = null and PRICE_isMissing = true
```

meaning that the column was absent from the GoldenGate trail image.

All configurable platform metadata is prefixed with `dptf_`. The formatter-controlled `before`, `after` and `_isMissing` fields are documented exceptions.

