# 7. Event deduplication

GoldenGate S3 delivery is at least once after failure recovery. A file or operation can therefore be replayed after a failure between upload and checkpoint advancement.

Spark should calculate:

```text
dptf_event_id =
SHA-256(
    dptf_source_system
    || dptf_source_database
    || dptf_source_object
    || dptf_trail_position
    || dptf_transaction_operation_seq
    || dptf_operation_type
)
```

Do not include:

```text
dptf_ingestion_ts
```

because GoldenGate’s current processing timestamp can change when the same trail operation is replayed. The trail position identifies the record’s location in the source trail.

The Bronze Iceberg table should deduplicate or `MERGE` on:

```text
dptf_event_id
```

