# 8. Simple partition watermark

No individual file manifest is required.

Use one watermark row per:

```text
source database
+ source schema
+ source table
+ hourly partition
```

## Table schema

```sql
CREATE TABLE platform_control.dptf_cdc_partition_watermark (
    dptf_pipeline_id             STRING NOT NULL,

    dptf_source_system           STRING NOT NULL,
    dptf_source_database         STRING NOT NULL,
    dptf_source_schema           STRING NOT NULL,
    dptf_source_table            STRING NOT NULL,

    dptf_partition_hour          TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
    dptf_partition_status        STRING NOT NULL,

    dptf_processing_run_id       STRING,
    dptf_record_count            BIGINT,

    dptf_max_source_csn          STRING,
    dptf_max_trail_position      STRING,

    dptf_processed_at            TIMESTAMP,
    dptf_error_message           STRING,

    dptf_created_at              TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
    dptf_updated_at              TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
)
USING iceberg
PARTITIONED BY (days(dptf_partition_hour));
```

## Logical key

```text
dptf_pipeline_id
+ dptf_source_database
+ dptf_source_schema
+ dptf_source_table
+ dptf_partition_hour
```

## Statuses

Only three statuses are necessary:

```text
PROCESSING
PROCESSED
FAILED
```

No file-level state, sealing state or S3 version metadata is maintained.

